{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For a US-listed equity ETF, budget **one-time launch costs** separately from seed capital: legal formation/registration and listing work, index licensing or custom methodology, initial platform/onboarding and connectivity, and launch/distribution setup. Seed assets are contributed capital used to establish the fund and support trading—not an expense; they remain fund assets, subject to market risk and any seed-share redemption.\n\nBudget recurring costs: management, fund administration/accounting, custody, transfer agency, index/license fees, listing/exchange and regulatory fees, audit, tax, legal/compliance, reporting, and platform/service-provider charges. Under a unitary fee, the sponsor generally pays covered operating expenses from its fee; identify exclusions (often brokerage, financing, taxes, extraordinary items) and who bears them under fund documents. Fund trading costs and portfolio transaction taxes reduce NAV; investors bear bid–ask spreads and their own platform charges.\n\nModel payer, timing, fixed/variable basis, and exclusions per contract—no universal quote applies. Break-even requires fee revenue (rate × average net assets) to cover sponsor-borne costs; positive retained margin requires revenue to exceed those costs, allowing for asset variability and waivers."}}
